<topic id="cf-change-admin-password">
  <title><?oxy_delete content="How to Change the Administration Page Password Change admin password Change fusion password" author="Gemma4" timestamp="20260408T120000+0000"?><?oxy_insert_start author="Gemma4" timestamp="20260408T120000+0000"?>How to Change the Administration Page Password<?oxy_insert_end?></title>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Change admin password</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Change fusion password</indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_dn5_dgk_54b"><?oxy_delete content="To change the password of the admin user (&lt;i&gt;fusion&lt;/i&gt;), follow these steps:" author="Gemma4" timestamp="20260408T120000+0000"?><?oxy_insert_start author="Gemma4" timestamp="20260408T120000+0000"?>To change the admin user (&lt;i&gt;fusion&lt;/i&gt;) password, follow these steps:<?oxy_insert_end?><ol
        id="ol_wmt_wtv_k4b">
        <li id="li_en5_dgk_54b">Run the following command to obtain the hashed form of the new
          password:<codeblock id="codeblock_adr_15v_k4b" outputclass="language-ini">cd /fusion
sudo docker-compose exec config-server nodejs /config-server/hashpwd.js my-new-password</codeblock></li>
        <li id="li_fn5_dgk_54b">Write the resulting output in
            the<filepath>/fusion/default-data/config/config-server/users.json</filepath> file.
          Replace the <codeph>password</codeph> field with the hashed password obtained in the
          previous step.</li>
        <li id="li_gn5_dgk_54b"><xref href="cf-restart.dita">Restart Content Fusion</xref>. </li>
      </ol></p>
  </body>
